  "slides": [
    {
      "page_title": "Committing: Auto, Sync, Async (cont.)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Two rules",
          "items": [
            "Commit only offsets whose side effects are durable",
            "Committing a partition you no longer own throws CommitFailedException",
            "That exception means you missed a rebalance"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "poll() Does Everything",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Not just a fetch: it joins the group",
            "It fires rebalance callbacks and drives coordination",
            "A consumer that stops polling is dead to the group",
            "Thread health is irrelevant, only polls count"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Two Failure Detectors"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Config",
            "Default",
            "Catches"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`heartbeat.interval.ms`",
              "3000",
              "cadence only"
            ],
            [
              "`session.timeout.ms`",
              "45000",
              "dead process"
            ],
            [
              "`max.poll.interval.ms`",
              "300000",
              "stuck processor"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Keep heartbeat at or below one third of session timeout",
            "Since KIP-62 heartbeats run on a background thread",
            "So the two detectors are fully independent",
            "Session timeout is wall clock between heartbeats"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Fetch Sizing"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`max.poll.records` default 500 caps records per poll",
            "Primary lever for keeping processing under the interval",
            "`fetch.min.bytes` and `fetch.max.wait.ms` trade latency for throughput",
            "`fetch.max.bytes`, `max.partition.fetch.bytes` bound memory per response"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Sizing rule",
          "text": "`max.poll.records` times worst-case per-record time must sit comfortably under `max.poll.interval.ms`."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Loop And Shutdown"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "java",
          "lines": [
            "while (running) {",
            "  var recs = consumer.poll(ofMillis(100));",
            "  process(recs);",
            "  consumer.commitAsync();",
            "}"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "The Poll Loop and Its Timeouts",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "wakeup()",
              "WakeupException",
              "commitSync()",
              "close(Duration)",
              "LeaveGroup"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Call `wakeup()` from another thread",
            "`poll()` throws `WakeupException`, catch it",
            "`close(Duration)` sends LeaveGroup",
            "Group rebalances now, not after the session timeout"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Threading"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "The consumer is NOT thread-safe",
            "One consumer per thread, or hand records to a worker pool",
            "With a pool you manage offsets yourself",
            "`pause()` partitions while workers lag",
            "Commit only below the lowest in-flight record"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Symptom To Cause",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Symptom",
            "Cause"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "CommitFailedException",
              "poll interval blown"
            ],
            [
              "Endless rebalance loop",
              "one slow member"
            ],
            [
              "Duplicates every deploy",
              "no revoke-commit, no `close()`"
            ],
            [
              "Idle, zero partitions",
              "more consumers than partitions"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Blown interval: lower `max.poll.records`, or raise the interval",
            "Slow member: find the record, add a per-record timeout",
            "Duplicates: graceful shutdown plus commit on revoke",
            "Idle: add partitions or shrink the fleet"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Offset Surprises"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Symptom",
            "Cause"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Replay after a quiet weekend",
              "retention plus `earliest`"
            ],
            [
              "Silent data skip",
              "`latest` on a new group"
            ],
            [
              "Lag on one partition",
              "hot-key producer skew"
            ],
            [
              "Reads stall",
              "hung open transaction"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "An idle weekend can beat `offsets.retention.minutes`",
            "New group: set `earliest` or seed offsets deliberately",
            "Hot key: change the key or write a custom partitioner",
            "Stalls only bite `read_committed` readers, at the Last Stable Offset"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Common Failure Modes and Fixes",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Static Membership Bites"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "FencedInstanceIdException: two pods share one `group.instance.id`",
            "Rebalance on every restart: boot slower than `session.timeout.ms`",
            "Fix: raise the timeout above real pod restart time"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Poison Pills"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "java",
          "lines": [
            "try { handle(rec); }",
            "catch (Exception e) {",
            "  log.error(\"dlq\", e);",
            "  dlq.send(rec);  // never re-loop",
            "}"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A record that always throws re-delivers forever",
            "try/catch per record, route to a dead-letter topic",
            "Catching, skipping and committing anyway is silent data loss",
            "If you skip, log it loudly"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Anti-Patterns"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Blocking network call inside the loop with no timeout",
            "That is the number-one cause of poll-interval eviction",
            "`Thread.sleep()` for backpressure",
            "Use `pause()` and `resume()` so heartbeats and polls continue"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Debug kit",
          "items": [
            "`--describe` for lag",
            "`--describe --state` for group state",
            "`--members --verbose` for assignment",
            "Metrics: `records-lag-max`, `commit-latency-avg`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Sizing",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Partitions = peak throughput divided by per-consumer throughput",
            "Then add headroom on top",
            "You can add partitions later, never remove them"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Config Checklist"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Set",
            "To"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`partition.assignment.strategy`",
              "CooperativeSticky, 2 phases"
            ],
            [
              "`group.instance.id`",
              "StatefulSet ordinal"
            ],
            [
              "`session.timeout.ms`",
              "above restart time"
            ],
            [
              "`enable.auto.commit`",
              "`false`"
            ],
            [
              "`max.poll.records`",
              "tune down first"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Kill auto-commit wherever a duplicate or a loss matters",
            "Commit explicitly after processing",
            "Shorter batches beat longer deadlines"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Design Checklist and Summary",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Code Checklist"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`ConsumerRebalanceListener`: commit on revoke, no commit on lost",
            "Shutdown hook plus `wakeup()`, always `close()`",
            "`close()` turns a 45-second stall into an instant rebalance",
            "Make every consumer idempotent"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Semantics Choice"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "Kafka to Kafka",
                "lines": [
                  "Transactional exactly-once",
                  "`sendOffsetsToTransaction()`",
                  "`read_committed`"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "Kafka to database",
                "lines": [
                  "Offsets in your DB txn",
                  "At-least-once plus idempotency",
                  "Simpler and cheaper"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Idempotency beats transactions in most systems",
            "Reach for exactly-once only for Kafka-to-Kafka pipelines",
            "Alert on lag trend and rebalance rate, not absolute lag"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
