  "caption": {
    "text": "Part 2 of KAFKA CONSUMER GROUPS. Your consumer group is not slow because Kafka is slow — it is slow because it keeps rebalancing. 10 pages on how partitions get assigned, why the poll loop is really a heartbeat, what a committed offset actually means (last processed + 1), and the exact configs that turn a 45-second stall into an instant handoff. Save it for the next CommitFailedException.",
